Command Purpose:
Displays information about your computer's wireless network adapter and its supported Wi-Fi capabilities.
To determine what wireless technologies your adapter supports.
Step 6: Enter the command: (netsh wlan show profiles).
Command Purpose: 
Lists the Wi-Fi network profiles saved on your windows computer.
To identify configured wireless network profiles.
Step 7: Enter the command: (Get-NetAdapter).
Command Purpose:
Displays your computer's network adapters.
To identify and check the status of your wireless network adapter.












Step 8: Enter the command: (Get-NetConnectionProfile).
Command Purpose: 
Displays information about the currently connected network profile.
To identify the current Wi-Fi network and its Windows network profile.













